  ==============================================================================
    LORRAX runtime — resolved startup configuration
  ==============================================================================
    This is rank 0 of 4, and it addresses 1 of the 4 devices in the job.
    jax.distributed.initialize() took its explicit form with coordinator_address='c207-013:13528', num_processes=4 and local_device_ids=None.
    The JAX platform resolved to 'cpu' on devices of kind 'cpu', from JAX_PLATFORMS='cpu', under jax 0.9.1 with 64-bit values enabled.
    The run's device mesh is 2x2 over axes ('x', 'y'), and its communicator cliques were warmed before the first physics jit.
    Bringing this stack up took 8.3 s in total: 5.5 s for the environment, jax.distributed and backend init, 0.7 s to build the mesh and warm its communicators, 2.1 s to arm the compile cache and 0.0 s to measure everything in this block.
    DEMOTION: GPU PJRT plugin discovery was skipped (JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu), so no CUDA library was loaded; the measured saving on a cold Frontera node is 76.9 s (job 7882076), and LORRAX_CPU_SKIP_GPU_PLUGINS=0 restores it.
    Demotions listed above are this rank's; a demotion that happened only on another rank is announced in that rank's own output and does not appear here.
    Multi-process CPU collectives run on the MPI implementation (JAX_CPU_COLLECTIVES_IMPLEMENTATION=mpi) through the MPItrampoline wrapper /work2/08271/jackmc/frontera/lorrax_mpiwrapper/install/lib64/libmpiwrapper.so.
    The MPI transport knobs resolved to LORRAX_MPI_FINALIZE_FIX='skip_atexit' and LORRAX_MPI_FORCE_THREAD_MAIN=None; the thread-main refusal is handled by warming the cliques from the main thread, so the wrapper override is not required.
    The XLA GPU pool knobs do not apply on the cpu backend, and that backend keeps no arena accounting, so no allocator figure is reported.
    The cpu FFI library loaded from /work2/08271/jackmc/frontera/lorrax_ffi_unified/build_host_PADFIX/liblorrax_ffi_host.so, selected by LORRAX_FFI_HOST_SO.
    FFI build provenance: /work2/08271/jackmc/frontera/lorrax_ffi_unified/build_host_PADFIX/liblorrax_ffi_host.so | rev d935ce703 | sha 13a0b667261e071a | built 2026-08-02T21:46:45Z | slate=on
    The LORRAX_BANDS_GEMM_FFI dial is unset and resolved to on, so the contract_bands right-GEMM contraction is routed through the FFI handler (the required layer).
    The LORRAX_FFT_FFI dial is unset and resolved to on, so the flat-k 3-D FFT helper path is routed through the FFI handler (the required layer).
    The LORRAX_FFT_FFI_FUSED dial is unset and resolved to on, so the fused IFFT-multiply-FFT tau kernel is routed through the FFI handler (the required layer).
    The distributed backends available for eigh on this mesh are distributed, native, scalapack; which one runs is the input-file key, not an environment variable.
    The distributed backends available for cholesky on this mesh are native, slate; which one runs is the input-file key, not an environment variable.
    The distributed backends available for solve_lu on this mesh are distributed, native, scalapack; which one runs is the input-file key, not an environment variable.
    This process is pinned to 28 schedulable CPUs, with OMP_NUM_THREADS='28', MKL_NUM_THREADS='28' and OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS='28'.
    Inside the FFI handlers the BLAS team size is LORRAX_MKLBLAS_THREADS=None for the batched GEMM, where unset means the ambient thread count, and LORRAX_SCALAPACK_MKL_THREADS=None for the ScaLAPACK handlers, where unset means a cap of 4 because pzheevd measured 11.28 s per q at 14 MKL threads against 0.463 s at 4.
    The JAX persistent compile cache is enabled at /scratch2/08271/jackmc/lorrax_jax_cache/np4, shared by all 4 ranks through the hit/miss agreement layer.
    The cache key includes every array shape, so a system size this machine has not run before misses every entry no matter how warm the cache looks.
    The fail-fast excepthook is installed, so an uncaught exception on any rank exits the step non-zero instead of leaving its peers blocked in a collective that rank will never join.
    glibc malloc tuning is in force with M_MMAP_THRESHOLD=1 MB and M_TRIM_THRESHOLD=128 MB, which is the mitigation for the per-r-chunk RSS ramp on long XLA:CPU runs.
